Wondwossen, his best friend and collaborator in mischief; Mr. Alula, their embattled teacher; Mr. Tadesse, full-time school director and part-time poacher; Ms. Yetaferu, the Orthodox Christian boarder who manages to find a saint to worship each day of the year and thus to avoid gainful employment; and Yeneta, the local priest who is privy to the languages of heaven and hell.\". \"Notes from the Hyena's Belly teems with the smells, sights, and sounds of life in the Horn of Africa - its violent, ingenious people and its underworld of screeching monkeys, lions, and hyenas. Part autobiography and part social history, this is an unforgettable portrait of a world where the boundaries of credulity are challenged daily. Out of this rich, sundrenched land where modern corruption rides ancient custom like a predator, Mezlekia crafts a world elegant in its aridity, extreme in its absurdity, and vast in its ironies.\"--BOOK JACKET.","publicationYear":2000,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Childhood and youth","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"History","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Burgerkrieg","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biographies","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Histoire","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-notes-from-the-hyena-s-belly-nega-mezlekia"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"op